# test: add online tests for Get-IRTEntraSignInLog

## Summary

`Get-IRTEntraSignInLog` had thorough offline tests but no live coverage. This
adds an Online-tagged Pester suite that runs the function against the real
Microsoft Graph sign-in logs endpoint, exercising the query/chunk/merge/sort
pipeline end-to-end rather than against mocks.

The guiding constraint was to mock as little as possible. Only three things are
mocked, and none of them sit on the data path:

- `Show-IRTEntraSignInLog` — captures the records the function produces so the
  tests can assert on them, without writing an Excel workbook or invoking the
  `ip_info` enrichment tool.
- `Write-IRT` / `Write-PSFMessage` — suppress console noise.

Everything else runs for real: the Graph SDK cmdlets
(`Get-MgBetaAuditLogSignIn`, `Get-MgAuditLogSignIn`) and the internal helpers
(`Update-IRTToken`, `Import-IRTModule`, `Get-DefaultDomain`,
`Resolve-DateRange`).

The file follows the structure already established by
`Get-IRTUnifiedAuditLog.Paths.Online.Tests.ps1`: each Context issues one cached
live query in its `BeforeAll` and shares the result across its `It` blocks to
keep the number of live Graph calls low.

## What's covered

- **`-UserObject` (interactive, 30 days)** — confirms the `UserId eq '<guid>'`
  filter reached Graph (every record belongs to the test user) and that the
  date window is honored.
- **`-AllUsers` (beta, 7 days)** — tenant-wide query; also captures a live
  source IP for the next context.
- **`-IpAddress`** — reuses the IP observed in the AllUsers result, so the
  originating record guarantees a hit; verifies the `ipAddress eq` filter.
  Skips cleanly if no IP was available.
- **`-NonInteractive`** — verifies the `signInEventTypes` clause reached Graph
  (`IsInteractive` is `$false` on every record).
- **`-Beta $false`** — exercises the v1.0 endpoint branch.
- **Date chunking** (`-Days 7 -ChunkDays 1`) — exercises the multi-chunk
  accumulate/merge/sort path and asserts newest-first ordering.
- **Absolute `-Start` / `-End` range**.

## Notes / assumptions

- The suite treats `IRT_TEST_USER_ID` as the authenticating account, so it
  always has recent interactive and non-interactive sign-in activity. This
  matches how the existing UAL online tests use the same variable.
- Assertions read the `UserId`, `IpAddress`, `IsInteractive`, and
  `CreatedDateTime` properties of the live records.

## Testing

- All applicable formatting checks pass against the new file (LineLength,
  ModuleSyntax, FormatOperator, NonASCIICharacters, BacktickContinuation,
  JoinPath, WriteVerboseDebug, PSSA).
- The online suite itself has not been run here, since it requires a live
  tenant session (`Connect-IRT`) and a valid `IRT_TEST_USER_ID`. Run with
  `.\Tests.ps1 Online` (add `-InteractiveAuth` if the test token cache is
  empty).
